<Base title="Privacy Policy — EGI" description="Learn how Elemonator Games Inc. collects, uses, and protects personal information.">
  <!-- Editable privacy policy page: headline and intro copy -->
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: August 25, 2026</em></p>
  <p>Elemonator Games Inc. ("EGI," "we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy applies to this website and to all games and apps we publish, including "Mine With Friends" and any future EGI titles, whether played directly on this site, embedded on a third-party platform, or distributed through a game portal. It explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. This policy is intended to satisfy the privacy-policy requirements of game distribution portals (e.g. Poki, CrazyGames) as well as general web and app privacy standards.</p>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: information collection details -->
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you provide directly:</strong> your name, email address, and message content when you use our contact form; any information you choose to share when you contact us for support, press, or partnership inquiries.</p>
    <p><strong>Automatically collected information:</strong> standard technical data such as IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating system, general location (e.g. country/region derived from IP), referring URLs, and pages or in-game screens visited. This is typically collected via standard web server and CDN logs even where no dedicated analytics tool is active.</p>
    <p><strong>Gameplay and multiplayer information:</strong> for multiplayer features (e.g. the presence overlay in "Mine With Friends"), we may process a display name or player identifier, session/room identifiers, connection data (including IP address, used to host the multiplayer session), and in-game progress or state needed to run the game.</p>
    <p><strong>Purchase information:</strong> in-game purchases (e.g. gems) are processed by our payment partner, Xsolla. We receive confirmation that a purchase was made and the item purchased, but we do not receive, process, or store your full payment card or billing details — those are handled directly by Xsolla under its own privacy policy.</p>
    <p><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> see our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for full details on the cookies and local storage used by this site and our games.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: how collected information is used -->
    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information above to operate and improve our website and games, run multiplayer and account-related features, process in-game purchases through our payment partner, respond to inquiries, show and measure advertising, detect and prevent abuse or fraud, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: advertising disclosure (Google AdSense) -->
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>This site and our "Mine With Friends" game use Google AdSense to show ads. Google and its partners may use cookies, device identifiers, and similar technologies to serve ads — including based on your prior visits to this or other websites — and to measure ad performance. You can review or change your ad consent choices at any time using the "Manage Ad Consent" link in the site footer, adjust ad personalization directly in your <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>, or learn more about how Google uses information from sites and apps that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: third-party service providers -->
    <h2>Third-Party Services We Use</h2>
    <p>We rely on trusted third-party providers to operate our site and games, each governed by its own privacy policy:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — advertising.</li>
      <li><strong>Xsolla</strong> — payment processing for in-game purchases.</li>
      <li><strong>Colyseus-based multiplayer infrastructure</strong> — hosts real-time multiplayer sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> — hosts this website.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — runs the serverless function behind our contact form.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers email notifications from our contact form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you play one of our games on a third-party portal or platform (for example, a game aggregator site), that platform's own privacy policy and data practices also apply to any data it collects directly, separately from this policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: children's privacy / COPPA statement -->
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our games are intended for a general audience and are not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your jurisdiction) without verifiable parental consent. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can remove it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: data retention -->
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain information only as long as needed for the purposes described in this policy, to provide our services, or to comply with legal obligations, after which it is deleted or anonymized.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: data protection and sharing statement -->
    <h2>Data Protection</h2>
    <p>We apply reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your information. We only share data with trusted service providers — such as those listed above — when needed to operate our site and games, or when required by law.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: international data transfers -->
    <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>Our service providers may process and store data in countries other than your own, including the United States and Canada. Where this occurs, we rely on our providers' contractual and technical safeguards to protect your information consistent with this policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: user choices and contact guidance -->
    <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of your personal data, and to object to or restrict certain processing (for example, under GDPR or similar laws in the EU/UK, or CCPA/CPRA in California — we do not sell personal information). You can exercise these rights, or ask us any question about this policy, by contacting us. You can also manage your ad consent choices at any time using the "Manage Ad Consent" link in the site footer, or disable cookies through your browser settings.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: policy update notice -->
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by updating the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of our site or games after changes take effect indicates acceptance of the revised policy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <!-- Editable privacy policy section: contact information -->
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy or your data can be sent to <a href="mailto:elemonatorgames@gmail.com">elemonatorgames@gmail.com</a>. See our <a href="/contact">Contact Information</a> page for more ways to reach us.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
